cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Eir, please cite the paper below and name the version you used."
title: "Eir: bond valence screening of crystal structures, with an integrity verdict"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Reeves-McLaren
    given-names: Nik
    affiliation: University of Sheffield
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1061-1230"
version: 2.0.46
date-released: 2026-11-11
abstract: >-
  Eir reads CIF files and asks of each structure whether it can be
  assessed at all and, if so, how well its bond valence sums agree with the
  formal valences. It returns an integrity verdict with the code that
  decided it, the bond valence sum of every site, the global instability
  index, and the evidence for each. This release is engine 2.0.46,
  packaged as eir-bvs 2.1.0.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SuperBladesman/Eir"
keywords:
  - crystallography
  - bond valence sum
  - global instability index
  - crystal structure validation
  - ICSD
  - CIF
  - data integrity
